  "impact": "The listed CVEs affect Linux kernel implementation code. This exact Ubuntu package contains exported userspace development headers and two documentation files, without kernel implementation, modules or executables. The headers remain required for first-use native model builds. Each upstream fix below was compared with the 990 installed package paths. Runtime image qualification independently verifies the files are regular headers/documentation and that the path manifest matches. This assessment covers this image package only; it makes no assertion about the host kernel.",
  "references": [
    "https://packages.ubuntu.com/noble/linux-libc-dev",
    "https://packages.ubuntu.com/noble/amd64/linux-libc-dev/filelist",
    "https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/kbuild/headers_install.html"
  ],
  "exported_header_change": {
    "cve": "CVE-2026-80668",
    "path": "include/uapi/linux/netfilter/nf_conntrack_common.h",
    "fix_commit": "b8b09dc2bf35a00d4e0556b5d6308c7b917ebda2",
    "reason": "The only changed exported-header path adds NF_CT_EXPECT_DEAD inside __KERNEL__. headers_install.sh removes this section with unifdef -U__KERNEL__ -D__EXPORTED_HEADERS__. Pre/post exported header bytes are identical; the race fix is in netfilter kernel code absent from this package.",
